---
import NidoLayout from "../../layouts/NidoLayout.astro";
---
<NidoLayout title="Nido — Local fees">
<div class="col-scroll pad fee-page">
<section id="fee-selector">
  <p class="eyebrow">Testnet · local fees</p><h1 class="disp">Your wallet pays its own way.</h1>
  <p>Choose your Nido, or create one with the usual passkey setup. Your wallet keeps F local, checks every action, and refills it within an on-chain Perch budget.</p>
  <div id="fee-accounts"></div><button id="fee-create" class="btn acc" disabled>Create a Nido with local fees</button>
  <p id="fee-select-status" role="status"></p>
</section>
<div id="fee-wallet" hidden>
<header><a href="/account/">← Your Nido</a> <span class="brand">nido <span>/ wallet-owned fees</span></span><span id="network-label" class="pill">Isolated local chain · fake XLM</span></header>
<section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Your fee key stays here</p><h1 style="font-size:48px">A little tank.<br>A firm refill limit.</h1><p class="lede">C approves the action. Your local F key pays the fee. When F is low, a reusable Perch policy refills only this registered F from the treasury’s allowance.</p></section>
<div id="network-scope" class="scope"><strong>Real local ledger execution.</strong> This route uses a deployed Perch fee policy, Perch authorization and WebAuthn contracts, the wallet’s WASI/Cedar check, and native XLM transfers. The bootstrap service supplies fake local funds; Turnkey is not connected.</div>
<section class="section"><div class="card"><p class="eyebrow">1 / Enroll once</p><h2 style="font-size:30px">One F. One lifetime budget.</h2><p id="enrollment-copy">Reuse this origin’s encrypted demo seed, or create one with a passkey. The local treasury funds the initial reserve separately and grants a 0.15 XLM refill allowance. F’s target is 1.10 XLM, including its reserve.</p><button id="budget-enroll" disabled>Register Perch fee policy</button><p class="small">The threshold equals the target in this teaching demo, so each small fee makes the next refill visible. Production would leave a wider gap. Initial funding and fees paid to bootstrap are outside this refill cap.</p><details><summary>Registered on-chain identities</summary><dl><dt>C · fixed-rule demo account using Perch</dt><dd id="budget-c">Not registered</dd><dt>F · local HD key / native fee account</dt><dd id="budget-f">Not registered</dd><dt>Reusable Perch fee policy</dt><dd id="budget-contract">Not registered</dd></dl></details></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="card"><p class="eyebrow">2 / Send an intent</p><h2 style="font-size:30px">Refill when needed, then act.</h2><p>The demo action increments a counter on chain. If F is below target, the wallet first asks you to authorize a separate refill. Each transaction uses the same enrolled passkey and the local U/F HD keys. The wallet refuses any envelope whose maximum fee exceeds 0.05 XLM.</p><button id="budget-run" disabled>Approve action · auto top-up if needed</button><div id="budget-message" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading your Nido fee wallet…</div>
<div class="result-row"><span>Budget</span><strong id="budget-state">Not registered</strong></div><div class="result-row"><span>F’s current XLM balance</span><strong id="budget-balance">—</strong></div><div class="result-row"><span>Total refilled / lifetime cap</span><strong id="budget-spent">—</strong></div><progress id="budget-meter" max="1500000" value="0" style="width:100%;accent-color:#0a6b75"></progress><div class="result-row"><span>Remaining contract budget</span><strong id="budget-remaining">—</strong></div><div class="result-row"><span>Remaining treasury token allowance</span><strong id="budget-allowance">—</strong></div><div class="result-row"><span>Confirmed demo actions</span><strong id="budget-uses">0</strong></div><div class="result-row"><span>Successful budget refills</span><strong id="budget-checks">0</strong></div><div class="result-row"><span>Wallet signing check</span><strong id="budget-runtime">Not run</strong></div><details><summary>WASI evidence for the latest envelope</summary><pre id="budget-evidence">Not run</pre></details><details open><summary>Transaction receipts</summary><ol id="budget-history" class="small" style="overflow-wrap:anywhere;padding-left:20px"></ol></details></div></section>
<section class="section"><h3>One passkey. A separate funding limit.</h3><p>The wallet asks C to execute the fixed refill adapter. Native Perch checks C’s owner passkey. The budget then computes the refill from F’s real balance and its remaining lifetime cap.</p><p class="small">Changing a Perch document or renewing the treasury allowance cannot reset the budget or change F. The budget has no recipient setter, reset or upgrade entry point.</p><details><summary>How this fits Perch dev</summary><p>Nido resolves your current native Perch owner rule before each approval. Production can give the adapter a dedicated document grant using existing function and authorization-root constraints. The reusable budget is the settlement component; there is no OZ policy callback or new fee-budget document keyword. This page uses your real document-managed Nido account. Nido still owns recovery, policy changes and account upgrades.</p></details></section>
<section class="section"><h3>What the proof says.</h3><p>For every input to the extracted Rust refill function, an accepted plan pays the registered recipient, increases cumulative spending by exactly that amount, and never exceeds the cap. It also requires a low balance and an unexpired budget. The contract exposes no destination, amount, reset or upgrade argument.</p><p class="small">Token transfers, authorization and failure rollback are checked in contract tests and local ledger execution. Lean does not prove the Soroban host, Perch, browser, compiler or cryptography. The cap applies to this contract’s refills—not bootstrap funds, unrelated deposits or all spending from F. F’s native key is still capable of signing elsewhere if the trusted wallet or seed is compromised.</p><p class="small">No silent renewal: when a refill cannot fit, it stops. Replenishing the SAC allowance does not reset spending. Budget renewal or F rotation would require a separately authorized design.</p></section>
<footer id="wallet-footer">Local-only demonstration · U and F remain in the wallet origin · no public deployment or Turnkey credentials</footer>
</div>
</div>
</NidoLayout>
<style>
.fee-page { max-width:850px; margin:auto; width:100%; }
.fee-page p {line-height:1.6;margin:12px 0;} header {display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-bottom:24px;}
.hero h1 {font-family:var(--font-display,serif);line-height:1.06;} .section {margin-top:24px;} .card,.scope {padding:24px;background:var(--paper,#fff);border:1px solid var(--line,#eddbc8);border-radius:20px;}
a{color:var(--acc,#0a6b75);} .pill{padding:6px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-size:12px;} .pill,.scope {background:var(--chip,#f9eee0);} .eyebrow {text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:700;}
button {padding:12px 18px;border-radius:12px;background:var(--acc,#0a6b75);color:white;cursor:pointer;border:0;font-weight:700;}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default;}
.result-row {display:flex;gap:16px;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#eddbc8);font-size:14px;}
code,pre {overflow-wrap:anywhere;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px;}details{margin-top:16px;}summary{cursor:pointer;} .small,footer{font-size:13px;color:var(--mut,#706259);}footer{margin:24px 0;}
.notice {margin:16px 0;padding:12px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--chip,#f9eee0);}.bad{color:#a22;}.good{color:#145953;}
#fee-accounts {display:grid;gap:12px;margin:24px 0;}#fee-selector h1{font-size:36px;} [hidden]{display:none!important;}
</style>
<script>
import { accountUrl, contractIdFromHostname, loadAccounts, loadAccountName, isContractId } from '@nidohq/passkey-sdk';
import { createNido } from '../../lib/createNido';
import { LOCAL_FEES_ENABLED } from '../../lib/network';
import { syncNidoStorageViaBridge } from '../../lib/nidoSharedStorage';
const status=document.getElementById('fee-select-status')!;
async function init() {
 if(!LOCAL_FEES_ENABLED)throw Error('Local fees are currently available in the testnet preview only.');
 const account=contractIdFromHostname(location.hostname);
 if(account){
  document.getElementById('fee-selector')!.hidden=true;
  document.getElementById('fee-wallet')!.hidden=false;
  const entry='/fee-demo/nido-fees.js';
  await import(/* @vite-ignore */ entry);
  return;
 }
 await syncNidoStorageViaBridge();
 for(const id of loadAccounts().filter(isContractId)) {
  const link=document.createElement('a');link.className='btn';link.href=accountUrl(location.host,id,'/fees/');
  link.textContent=loadAccountName(id)||`${id.slice(0,8)}…${id.slice(-6)}`;document.getElementById('fee-accounts')!.append(link);
 }
 (document.getElementById('fee-create') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled=false;
 document.getElementById('fee-create')!.onclick=()=>{
  const url=new URL(createNido(location.host),location.href);url.searchParams.set('fees','1');location.assign(url);
 };
}
init().catch(error=>{status.textContent=error.message; const message=document.getElementById('budget-message');if(message){message.textContent=error.message;message.classList.add('bad');}});
</script>
